# Wave: v0.10.5-legacy-decisions W9
# Covers: at (e?(var x)) body — payload binding names the emission payload.
#         Ruling: implemented (Wave 6 W9, legacy F4).
#
# Semantics: `at (e?(var payload)) body` desugars so the body closure has
#   one formal parameter named `payload`.  When `e!(42)` fires, 42 is
#   passed into R[0] of the body strand before it runs.  The body can then
#   reference `payload` as a local.
#
# Note: single-line body form required; REPL processes one line at a time.
#
# Activated: 2026-05-26 as part of v0.10.5-legacy-decisions W9.

var e = Event.new()
var result = 0
at (e?(var payload)) { Realm.result = payload }
e!(42)
Realm.result
[00000000] <event>
[00000000] 0
[00000000] nil
[00000000] nil
[00000000] 42
